@startuml

title Multiple simultaneous games

participant Client1
participant Client2
participant Server
participant Client3
participant Client4

group Game A
Client1->Server: CreateGameRequest(Game A)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(Game created)
Client1->Server: JoinGameRequest(Game A)
Client2->Server: JoinGameRequest(Game A)
Client1->Server: SubscribeGameRequest(Game A)
Client2->Server: SubscribeGameRequest(Game A)
end

group Game B
Client3->Server: CreateGameRequest(Game B)
Server-->Client3: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(Game created)
Client3->Server: JoinGameRequest(Game B)
Client4->Server: JoinGameRequest(Game B)
Client3->Server: SubscribeGameRequest(Game B)
Client4->Server: SubscribeGameRequest(Game B)
end

par command in Game A
Client1->Server: ChooseOfferRequest(Game A)
Server-->Client1: GameViewUpdate(Game A)
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(Game A)
else command in Game B
Client3->Server: ChooseCardRequest(Game B)
Server-->Client3: GameViewUpdate(Game B)
Server-->Client4: GameViewUpdate(Game B)
end

note over Client1, Client4
The server owns one independent GameSession per game name.
Commands and updates are delivered only to that session's subscribers.
end note

@enduml
